-- title:
--   Descent of an absolutely irreducible representation over a finite field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $L$ a finite field equipped with a $K$-algebra structure, and write $K' = \mathrm{range}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ K\ L)$ for the image subring of $K$ in $L$. Let $n$ be a nonempty finite index type with decidable equality, $G$ a group, and $\varphi \colon G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(L)$ a group homomorphism. Assume two things: first, the $L$-span of the set of matrices $\{\varphi(g) : g \in G\}$, taken inside $M_n(L)$ after forgetting invertibility, is all of $M_n(L)$ (Burnside's spanning condition); second, for every $g \in G$ and every index $i$, the $i$-th coefficient of the characteristic polynomial of the matrix $\varphi(g)$ lies in $K'$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a group homomorphism $\rho \colon G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(K')$ and of a single matrix $Q \in \mathrm{GL}_n(L)$ such that for all $g \in G$ the equality $Q^{-1}\,\varphi(g)\,Q = \rho(g)$ holds in $M_n(L)$, the right-hand side being the entrywise image of $\rho(g)$ under the inclusion $K' \hookrightarrow L$. Thus $\varphi$ becomes, after one fixed conjugation, a representation with entries in the subfield $K'$.
--
--   This is the absolutely irreducible case of Deligne–Serre, Lemme 6.13, in the form where Burnside's spanning hypothesis is stated explicitly and the coefficient field $L$ is finite; it is the descent step that produces a model of a mod-$\ell$ representation over the subfield generated by its traces and determinants. It is used in the proof of [`ModularCurve.exists_semisimple_descent_of_trace_det_mem_range_finite`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_semisimple_descent_of_trace_det_mem_range_finite), and its own proof invokes the Brauer–Nesbitt statement [`BrauerNesbitt.exists_linearEquiv_of_span_range_eq_top_of_trace_eq`](thm.html#BrauerNesbitt.exists_linearEquiv_of_span_range_eq_top_of_trace_eq).
